            <ArticleTitle>Thigh pain--an unusual presentation of ruptured appendicitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>102-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case in a 56-year-old female with a perforated retrocaecal appendicitis presenting as a large right thigh abscess. We discuss the diagnosis and treatment and the importance to refer early to a general surgeon if suspected.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
